{
  "kanji": "重",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 重\ntitle: heavy; piled up\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 里\nradicalNumber: 166\nonyomi: [ジュウ, チョウ]\nkunyomi: [え, おも.い, おも.り, おも.なう, かさ.ねる, かさ.なる, おも]\ndistractors: [車, 動, 東]\n---\n\n# 重 — heavy; piled up\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 里 (no. 166) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n重 can indicate **weight**, **importance**, or **things layered on one another**.\nA heavy bag and overlapping events use different words even though both contain 重.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture the horizontal strokes as layers stacked on a central support,\nmaking a heavy pile. This is a mnemonic for the modern shape, not verified history.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; the metadata preserves all source on and kun readings.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ジュウ | on | 体重 たいじゅう (body weight); 重要 じゅうよう (important) |\n| チョウ | on | 貴重 きちょう (precious; valuable) |\n| おも.い | kun | [重い](../words/重い.md) おもい (heavy) |\n| かさ.なる | kun | 重なる かさなる (overlap; be piled up) |\n| かさ.ねる | kun | 重ねる かさねる (stack; repeat) |\n| え | kun | 二重まぶた ふたえまぶた (double eyelid), 八重桜 やえざくら (double-flowered cherry) |\n| おも.り | kun | 重り おもり (weight; sinker), 釣りの重り つりのおもり (a fishing sinker) |\n| おも.なう | kun | archaic, dictionary-only: \"to take seriously\"; not needed |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [重い](../words/重い.md) おもい — heavy; serious\n- 体重 たいじゅう — body weight\n- 重要 じゅうよう — important\n- 重ねる かさねる — put one on top of another; repeat\n\n## Notes\n\nThe weight opposite of 重い is 軽い（かるい）, \"light.\" Do not substitute 重い for every English use\nof \"important\": 重要な（じゅうような）is useful for importance without a sense of burden.\n\n[車](車.md) also has a central vertical stroke and several horizontal strokes; check the top and bottom.\n[動](動.md) contains the shape 重 with [力](力.md) on the right.\n",
